  "lawGrade": "LOCKED",
  "lawGradeScale": "v4 law grading scale (native canon scale, strongest first): DERIVED, LOCKED, MAPPED, PARTIAL, SPLIT, OPEN, DEFINITIONAL. Mapping to C0-C6 unruled - tracked as OI-0011.",
  "statementTechnical": "Weak-force three-body decay n -> p + e- + anti-nu_e (Fermi theory). Canonical structural result: whole = broken + visible_damage + invisible_loss, with the total conserved; when visible_damage -> 0 (suppression), invisible_loss becomes maximal - it absorbs the remainder. 'Suppression is not repair.' Canonical grade LOCKED - second strongest law ('nothing was added'): moral damage is conserved; it can be redirected but not destroyed; hiding damage transfers it to the invisible channel. The theological terminus of transfer is the Cross. Open warnings (canonical): psi^5 dimensional repair still open; the 192pi^3 transfer requires genuine three-body phase-space structure; P_will double-count risk remains. Four conservation/limitation results converge: Newton's Third Law, the Second Law, angular momentum conservation, Kolmogorov uncomputability.",
  "statementPlain": "You cannot delete damage - you can only move it. Hide it and it goes underground, maximal and invisible, but the total never changes. That is the conservation structure of three-body decay, and canon locks it because, like Law 5, nothing was inserted. The structure is formalized in Lean (receipt external to this repo). What remains a bridge claim - named, not proven - is the theological identification: that the only terminus where the transferred cost finally lands is the Cross. Three dimensional-repair warnings stay open in canon and are carried on this atom.",
  "mathematicalForm": "whole = broken + visible_damage + invisible_loss; total conserved; visible_damage -> 0 => invisible_loss maximal",
  "mathFormNormal": "whole = broken + visible_damage + invisible_loss; total conserved; visible_damage -> 0 => invisible_loss maximal",
